lass=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/ranges/swap\"><span class=\"kw2874\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">swap</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>g1, g2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// heterogeneous swap supported</span>\n    print<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"g\"</span>, g1, g2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> h1<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">27</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, h2<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">28</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/ranges/swap\"><span class=\"kw2874\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">swap</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>h1, h2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    print<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"h\"</span>, h1, h2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>a1{ 13 14 }, a2{ 10 11 12 }\nb1{ 18 19 20 }, b2{ 15 16 17 }\nd1{ 24 25 26 }, d2{ 21 22 23 }\ng1{ 4 5 6 }, g2{ 1 2 3 }\nh1 = 28, h2 = 27</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/swappable\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swappable</span><span>swappable_with</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specifies that a type can be swapped or that two types can be swapped with each other <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(concept)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swap</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps the values of two objects <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Customization point objects","id":"Customization_point_objects"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::swap","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Exchanges the values referenced by t and u."},{"label":"Customization point objects","note":"The name ranges::swap denotes a customization point object, which is a const function object of a literal semiregular class type."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"swappable, swappable_with","note":"specifies that a type can be swapped or that two types can be swapped with each other"},{"label":"swap","note":"swaps the values of two objects"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":728,"codeBlockCount":2}
